00:20:56.321 --> 00:20:58.423
that was being pitched
in front of me.

00:20:58.423 --> 00:21:01.359
-The longer you do this job,
you know there's no bad movies.

00:21:01.359 --> 00:21:03.094
[ Laughter ]
-I love it.

00:21:03.094 --> 00:21:06.264
I love watching you
interview people so much

00:21:06.264 --> 00:21:09.368
just to see -- I can see it.
It's such a suppressed glint

00:21:09.368 --> 00:21:12.304
in your eye of,
"Well, congratulations."

00:21:12.304 --> 00:21:14.606
[ Laughter ]
-How dare you!

00:21:14.606 --> 00:21:17.142
Don't give up the game.
[ Laughter ]

00:21:17.142 --> 00:21:19.344
-"'Shazam! 2' looks great."
-No, no.

00:21:19.344 --> 00:21:22.213
-"Coming to a theater near you."
[ Laughter ]

00:21:22.213 --> 00:21:23.848
-It does look great.
-It does look good.

00:21:23.848 --> 00:21:25.751
It does look good.
-How dare you.

00:21:25.751 --> 00:21:28.787
How dare you use
a recent and specific example.

00:21:28.787 --> 00:21:30.822
[ Laughter ]

00:21:30.822 --> 00:21:33.157
-I'm sorry.
I was -- I swear.

00:21:33.157 --> 00:21:35.927
I -- I swear to you.

00:21:35.927 --> 00:21:39.130
I swear, my mind was going
through a bunch of things.

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:40.732
And it was right in the front.

00:21:40.732 --> 00:21:43.334
I did think,
"Not the best example."

00:21:43.334 --> 00:21:44.902
-Yeah, yeah.
-Ii mean, yes, the best example,

00:21:44.902 --> 00:21:46.604
but not for now.
[ Laughter ]

00:21:46.604 --> 00:21:49.440
And then I drew a blank.
You're right. It's a problem.

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:50.575 line:0%
-When did you make
the decision

00:21:50.575 --> 00:21:53.278 line:0%
to do a coronavirus deep dive

00:21:53.278 --> 00:21:54.379 line:0%
because you didn't have
a lot of planning?

00:21:54.379 --> 00:21:56.480 line:0%
-So, I guess the answer
to that is,

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:58.183 line:0%
it was atypical for us

00:21:58.183 --> 00:22:00.918 line:0%
because we decided
relatively early in our week,

00:22:00.918 --> 00:22:02.720 line:0%
and we did have
something else planned.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:04.790
But occasionally,
there are weeks

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.992
when if we have something
very timeless

00:22:06.992 --> 00:22:09.293
and maybe dry
that we've been working on,

00:22:09.293 --> 00:22:10.395
like something like we've done,

00:22:10.395 --> 00:22:12.330
like mobile home financing
in the past,

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:15.733
there are certain weeks, like,
I don't know, this week,

00:22:15.733 --> 00:22:17.569
where it's a little harder
to say,

00:22:17.569 --> 00:22:19.070
"I know that, you know,
coronavirus

00:22:19.070 --> 00:22:23.975
is spreading across the world
in borderline pandemic fashion,

00:22:23.975 --> 00:22:28.380
but I really need to talk
about mobile home financing."

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.714
It's a really hard sell
to be like,

00:22:29.714 --> 00:22:33.184
"You need to? You need to
or you want to?"

00:22:33.184 --> 00:22:35.519
in a needlessly
contrarian manner.

00:22:35.519 --> 00:22:39.257
So yeah, so we decided at
the start of our working week,

00:22:39.257 --> 00:22:40.892
and so we crashed it
pretty quickly.

00:22:40.892 --> 00:22:42.260
-And how do you feel right now?

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:45.397
Do you think that
we are suitably panicked?

00:22:45.397 --> 00:22:46.764
Do you think
we're over-panicked?

00:22:46.764 --> 00:22:47.799
-As people?
-Yeah.

00:22:47.799 --> 00:22:49.067
-It's on a person-to-person
basis.

00:22:49.067 --> 00:22:52.236
It depends --
Like, from a scale of 1 to 10,

00:22:52.236 --> 00:22:55.407
it depends what your regular
level of panic is on a good day.

00:22:55.407 --> 00:22:56.241
-Yeah.

00:22:56.241 --> 00:22:58.142
-Me, I'm at a regular 6 or 7.

00:22:58.142 --> 00:22:59.644
-Yeah.
-So...

00:22:59.644 --> 00:23:02.881
So this, you probably
have to go up a notch

00:23:02.881 --> 00:23:05.350
from wherever you were,
but not too much.

00:23:05.350 --> 00:23:07.018
That's the thing.
You've got to try and balance.

00:23:07.018 --> 00:23:09.153
Basically, just don't be
an idiot either way.

00:23:09.153 --> 00:23:10.521
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:23:10.521 --> 00:23:13.791
-My my wife is very
germ-averse to begin with.

00:23:13.791 --> 00:23:14.993
-In general, right?

00:23:14.993 --> 00:23:16.995
-Yeah, in general.
Right. Whereas I'm not.

00:23:16.995 --> 00:23:19.164
So I think most of her stress --
-I love germs.

00:23:19.164 --> 00:23:21.332
-I can't get enough of them.

00:23:21.332 --> 00:23:23.535
-Just looking
for super immunity,

00:23:23.535 --> 00:23:25.870
licking poles in the subway.

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:27.505
-That's the way I feel.
-[ Shouts indistinctly ]

00:23:27.505 --> 00:23:29.674
-I feel pretty strong
about that.

00:23:29.674 --> 00:23:31.576
I feel like my --
But that's the thing.

00:23:31.576 --> 00:23:33.378
She's always calling
and she's like, "Where are you?"

00:23:33.378 --> 00:23:35.012
And I'm like, "I'm at dinner."
She's like, "No, you're not.

00:23:35.012 --> 00:23:38.416
I can see you outside.
You're in the gutters." Yeah.

00:23:38.416 --> 00:23:41.553
-"Are you in Times Square again,
inhaling around Elmo?"

00:23:41.553 --> 00:23:43.555
-[ Laughs ]

00:23:43.555 --> 00:23:45.022
So, yeah, I think
her bigger concern

00:23:45.022 --> 00:23:46.357
is, like,
what I'm going to bring home

00:23:46.357 --> 00:23:47.792
as opposed to, like, her, yeah.

00:23:47.792 --> 00:23:49.460
-I think everyone's
going to have to wrestle

00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:53.497
