it's too late?

00:24:50.822 --> 00:24:53.891
-When does anyone
give you a stock tip?

00:24:53.891 --> 00:24:55.961
Seth, I know
you're a busy guy, but --

00:24:55.961 --> 00:24:58.763
-I always have lunch
at steakhouses.

00:24:58.763 --> 00:25:00.398
Yeah, exclusively.

00:25:00.398 --> 00:25:02.434
I take a full three-hour
steakhouse lunch.

00:25:02.434 --> 00:25:03.935
No, but, like,
even when you see it, like,

00:25:03.935 --> 00:25:06.538
I can't believe when people
watch CNBC or, you know,

00:25:06.538 --> 00:25:08.506
like, if you're watching
the news and a guy's saying,

00:25:08.506 --> 00:25:09.673
"Buy this stock,"
it's too late.

00:25:09.673 --> 00:25:11.109
-Yes.
-Right?

00:25:11.109 --> 00:25:13.378
I feel the same way about when
people say stock up on rice.

00:25:13.378 --> 00:25:15.746
Like, by the time I hear it,
the rice is gone.

00:25:15.746 --> 00:25:18.850
-That's right.
No question. Yeah, no question.

00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:21.085
If ever advice is going out
that you know you are

00:25:21.085 --> 00:25:23.922
walking into the Duane Reade,
it has empty shelves.

00:25:23.922 --> 00:25:25.490
-Yeah.

00:25:25.490 --> 00:25:27.158
Like if I went now,
I'd come back with, like,

00:25:27.158 --> 00:25:28.559
one orange Gatorade.

00:25:28.559 --> 00:25:30.462
I'd be like,
"It's all they had left, honey."

00:25:30.462 --> 00:25:31.897
-That's right.
I don't think -- Yeah.

00:25:31.897 --> 00:25:34.732
For the stock market or for,
you know, basic human hygiene,

00:25:34.732 --> 00:25:36.067
I've never moved fast enough.

00:25:36.067 --> 00:25:37.401
-Yeah.

00:25:37.401 --> 00:25:39.270
-No one has ever given me
a stock tip.

00:25:39.270 --> 00:25:41.673
-You know, I really --
now, I shouldn't have told you,

00:25:41.673 --> 00:25:43.174
'cause when they give me
the tips,

00:25:43.174 --> 00:25:46.244
