00:26:42.233 --> 00:26:44.268
-We were goofing hard.

00:26:44.268 --> 00:26:48.539
-...about the fact that
the first coronavirus case

00:26:48.539 --> 00:26:51.208
had just been confirmed
in New York City.

00:26:51.208 --> 00:26:54.345
And goof away, we were,
you know,

00:26:54.345 --> 00:26:56.815
slightly out of nervousness,
I think.

00:26:56.815 --> 00:26:58.148
-Sure, sure, sure.
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:26:58.148 --> 00:27:02.353
That's what what I was doing.
-Certainly. Certainly.

00:27:02.353 --> 00:27:04.755
Not a zero amount
of misplaced confidence.

00:27:04.755 --> 00:27:07.959
I remember leaving here
thinking, "Goofs well done,

00:27:07.959 --> 00:27:08.960
fun was had."

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.028
-Absolutely.

00:27:10.028 --> 00:27:11.596
-I got back to
my apartment building,

00:27:11.596 --> 00:27:13.064
and there was
an ambulance outside,

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:16.267
and I thought, "I have [bleep]
misjudged this situation."

00:27:16.267 --> 00:27:17.602
Oh [bleep]

00:27:17.602 --> 00:27:20.204
-Yeah.
-And it hadn't even been on TV.

00:27:20.204 --> 00:27:21.873
I was literally sitting
at home thinking,

00:27:21.873 --> 00:27:24.575
"I don't even want to watch
what I just said,

00:27:24.575 --> 00:27:27.011
'cause I think things
have shifted a little."

00:27:27.011 --> 00:27:30.014
So, it is very nice to be back.
-Yeah.

00:27:30.014 --> 00:27:31.882
-And I'm going to be
very careful with how

00:27:31.882 --> 00:27:34.586
